  "conclusion": "Replacing responder delay(1) with yield-only collapses RX-done IRQ-to-handler latency from hundreds of microseconds with an approximately 1 ms phase range to single-digit microseconds, and collapses the corresponding RTT modulation. Restoring delay(1) restores the broad IRQ-to-handler/RTT structure. Under this firmware and bench setup, the fixed 1 ms responder loop sleep is therefore a dominant causal contributor to the observed approximately 1 ms RTT modulation.",
  "boundary": "This does not prove delay(1) is the sole source of all latency or jitter. Samples are sequential, the first sample has startup effects, A2 RF levels drifted, and the diagnostic cross-clock residual is not propagation delay. No range, NLOS, interference or deployment-loss claim follows from this experiment."
